RISC3D test kit 22 (prototype, 14 November 2026)
================================================

TORCS through RISC3D: the car plain yellow and the scenery smeared. Kit
21's log showed no glActiveTexture at all from TORCS, but riscos-mesa
has checked that those calls do reach RISC3D, and TORCS on RISC OS runs
with one texture unit unless -M is given, so that was probably not it.
This kit's rol-3d (0.11, in riscos-risc3d 0.11-1) also logs every
texture TORCS uploads, level by level, and its filter settings. A
texture with a level missing or the wrong size is drawn without its
picture, which would give exactly that yellow car.

Steps
-----
 1. Copy RISC3DTest to HardDisc4 (unzip it there, replacing kit 21).
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.11-1_arm64.deb
    It restarts rol-3d itself. Don't reload the modules.
 3. In RiSH's Root shell:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/uploads memory
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/check on
 4. Run TORCS through RISC3D: start a race, drive for half a minute,
    then quit TORCS.
 5. If you have it: riscos-mesa's test, MESA/tests/
    riscos-mesa-multitex-test1.zip: double-click its Run.
 6. In RiSH's Root shell:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/check off
    and copy /riscos/3d/log.txt to the Mac.

